For the symbolic mode parser, let me handle the "who omitted" + umask interaction carefully:

When who is omitted:
- `+perm`: add only the ordinary bits not in umask. Special bits (s, t) are always added.
- `-perm`: remove only the ordinary bits not in umask. Special bits (s, t) are always removed.
- `=perm`: replace ordinary bits with (perm & ~umask). Special bits: set if in perm, cleared if not.

When who is explicit (including 'a'):
- `+perm`: add all bits (ordinary and special)
- `-perm`: remove all bits (ordinary and special)
- `=perm`: replace ordinary bits with perm. Special bits: set if in perm, cleared if not.

The key difference is the umask filtering on ordinary bits for omitted who.

